ptions, []string, error), processFiles, stub functions that panic(\"not implemented\")\n     - Manual arg parsing with parseShortFlag helper and flagValue helper\n     - Uses bufio.NewWriter for buffered stdout\n\n   - `pkg/sys` contract (from package_contracts in prompt):\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - signature: `func InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was about to begin writing code when interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified the contract pattern from cmd/cut/main.go to replicate for paste\n   - Analyzed srd027-paste to identify all flags: -d (delimiter list), -s (serial mode)\n   - Task description mentions \"zero-terminated mode\" as a flag to define, though SRD doesn't explicitly list -z\n   - Core operations identified: parallel merge, serial mode, delimiter parsing/cycling\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task specification including role definition, repository file listing, full project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/acceptance criteria/design decisions, shared protocols, and package contracts. The core request is: implement task #5280 \"[stitch] cmd/paste (contract)\" by creating cmd/paste/main.go as a stub/contract implementation.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/paste/main.go` with:\n     - Copyright header and package comment referencing srd027-paste\n     - options struct with delimiter, serial, zeroTerminated fields\n     - main() calling sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() first, then parseArgs, then dispatch\n     - parseArgs() for manual flag parsing (-d, -s, -z, --, etc.)\n     - parseDelimiters() stub for escape sequence handling\n     - pasteParallel() stub for parallel merge of fi